263
00:15:58.450 --> 00:15:59.650
That'd be my dream."

264
00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.120
Are you always this sarcastic?

265
00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.090
Always?
No, that's a strong word.

266
00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:06.260
Not always. Usually.

267
00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.700
I'm sorry. It's just, um...

268
00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.500
It's just been me and my mom

269
00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.500
since my dad died last year,
so yeah.

270
00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.240
I'm sorry.

271
00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.640
I don't really
think about it much anymore.

272
00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:19.410
What about you?

273
00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.810
Well, I never knew my mom,

274
00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:25.080
and we're always moving
from one town to the next.

275
00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.510
That really sucks.

276
00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.120
It's fine.

277
00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.290
Hey,

278
00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:38.160
can I ask you something
really serious, Hannah?

279
00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:40.030
Yeah. What?

280
00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.470
How do we get down?

281
00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.170
I'm serious. Is there a plan?

282
00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.310
No.
How do you normally get down?

283
00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.170
You can't. You're stuck.

284
00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.710
Wow, I can't believe

285
00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.580
you ate that cotton candy.

286
00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:59.210
And you know what's scary

287
00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:02.480
is it actually tasted
kind of fine.

288
00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.860
So, uh, thanks for tonight.

289
00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.860
That was the least terrible time
I've had here.

290
00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:15.460
Oh, Zach. That's so sweet.

291
00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.770
That's... I... Really.

292
00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.500
Okay.

293
00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.770
Hey, Hannah. I'm...

294
00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.540
I'm probably gonna
take out the trash

295
00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:26.340
on Tuesdays and Thursdays.

296
00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:29.280
So, you know, you feel like
creeping up on someone,

297
00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.810
that works for me.

298
00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.480
All right. I'll keep that
in mind, scaredy-cat.

299
00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:34.680
Hannah!

300
00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.350
What are you doing out here?

301
00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:38.720
I'm so sorry.

302
00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.760
This is your last warning.

303
00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:42.790
You stay away from us,

304
00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.590
or something very bad
will happen.

305
00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.260
I believe you.

306
00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.500
"What is X?"

307
00:17:58.670 --> 00:17:59.840
What is X?

308
00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.480
Dad, it's not a big deal.

309
00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.210
Hannah, you have to understand...

310
00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.750
I don't have to understand
anything.

311
00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.780
We were just talking.
Why can't I have friends?

312
00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:09.250
- You know why!
- That is not fair!

313
00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.790
You can't just lock me up
all the time.

314
00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.820
You are never allowed
to see that boy!

315
00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.560
You understand me? Ever!

316
00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:16.460
Dad, please calm down.

317
00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.660
- Hannah.
- No! Aah!

318
00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.740
What?

319
00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:48.860
What? I heard a scream.

320
00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.590
Is Hannah okay?
There was no scream.

321
00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:52.290
You didn't hear anything.
Get out of here

322
00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.330
or the last scream you hear
will be your own.

323
00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.760
No. Wait, wait...

324
00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:01.600
Mom.

325
00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.910
Hey, Mom. Mom. Mom.
Oh, hey, sweetie.

326
00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.840
Hey, how do you feel
about quinoa for dinner?

327
00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.380
Mom, Hannah's in trouble.

328
00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.410
Oh, who's Hannah?

329
00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.980
<i>Madison County 911.</i>

330
00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:17.320
Hi, yes. Uh, I live on Monroe.
Um...

331
00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.720
Uh, it's an emergency, I think.
Zach, what's going on?

332
00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:23.320
Yeah. Maybe possibly a domestic
disturbance. I don't know.

333
00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.470
You're under arrest!
Oh! Whoa, whoa, whoa.

334
00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:34.670
I love that enthusiasm.
I love that. Keep it.

335
00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:36.240
But we're just...
We're not there yet.

336
00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.240
Hello, sir.
My name's Officer Stevens.

337
00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:40.880
This is Training Officer Brooks.
I'm sorry about that before.

338
00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.380
You don't need to be sorry.

339
00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.550
- You're doing great.
- Really?

340
00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:48.620
We got a call about a possible
10-16 at your residence.

341
00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.350
Which is...?

342
00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.650
Um... Don't tell me.

343
00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:54.790
It's a domestic disturbance.

344
00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.720
Absolutely right. Really?

345
00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.430
Yeah. You're absolutely right.

346
00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.460
Strange, because I've been here
alone all night

347
00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.730
and I haven't heard a thing.
No, no, he's lying.

348
00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:05.400
Where's Hannah?
I know it was her screaming.

349
00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.300
Okay, yes. Hannah's my daughter,

350
00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.940
and she's been staying with me
for a while

351
00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:12.370
while her mother
sorted a few things out

352
00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.880
with her new husband. Ah, yeah.

353
00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.980
She flew back to London
yesterday morning.

354
00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:18.910
All right, well,
that checks out.

355
00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.850
Apologies, sir.
Thank you for your time.

356
00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.750
We're sorry for the disturbance.

357
00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.290
Surround sound.

358
00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.400
I didn't know being
an audiophile was a crime.

359
00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.800
Being a what... A what-a-phile?

360
00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.870
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

361
00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.670
That just means that he is
a connoisseur

362
00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.400
of high-end audio equipment.

363
00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.340
Oh.

364
00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.710
Hi. I'm so sorry.
We haven't properly met.

365
00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.680
I'm Gale Cooper,
your new neighbor.

366
00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.540
It's a beautiful home you have.

367
00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.310
Pleasure's mine. Thank you so
much for stopping by

368
00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.320
and bringing your delightful son
and the police.

369
00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:57.320
Again, I'm so sorry.

370
00:20:57.350 --> 00:20:58.820
Apologies for this, sir.

371
00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:00.050
We hate coming into the home

372
00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:01.960
of an upstanding citizen
such as yourself.

373
00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.360
Really sorry. I mean, obviously,
you're not doing anything...

374
00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:07.500
If you would like
to press charges,

375
00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.700
we would love to help you.

376
00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:11.430
Hannah! Hannah!

377
00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:12.730
Whoa! Hannah!

378
00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:14.000
Hold on, big guy. No, no!

379
00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.670
Just look upstairs. Trust me.

380
00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.040
Should I tase him?
I'll tase him.

381
00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:18.940
I like that moxie,
but we're gonna hold off.

382
00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.740
You have any idea
what the penalty is

383
00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.040
for filing a false
police report?

384
00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.680
Three years. Close.

385
00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:25.050
It's actually a written warning.

386
00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.580
Hold on, hold on. Mom, tell me
you don't believe him.

387
00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.020
Surround sound? Seriously?

388
00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.090
Zach, enough. Go home.

389
00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.700
Oh, officers. I'm so sorry.

390
00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.030
It's all right, ma'am.

391
00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.930
I feel like we should recommend

392
00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:45.530
a good treatment center
for your son.

393
00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.740
Yeah. That kid's on drugs.
That kid is on drugs.

394
00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:51.040
Good night.

395
00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:52.740
Gale.

396
00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:54.510
It's Lorraine.

397
00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:55.680
I can see you.

398
00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.080
It's your sister.

399
00:21:57.110 --> 00:22:00.010
Hi. Thanks for coming. Hi.

400
00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:02.150
I have to chaperone the dance
at the high school.

401
00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:04.020
I don't wanna leave Zach alone
tonight.

402
00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:07.890
Gale. He's a teenage boy
having a hard time adjusting.

403
00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:09.090
You know what he needs?

404
00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:12.090
A night in with his aunt,
BeDazzling.

405
00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:13.160
Duh.

406
00:22:13.190 --> 00:22:15.030
Oh, thanks.
I hate fighting with him.

407
00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:17.900
I know. It'll get better.
Just give it some time.

408
00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:20.500
All right. Kit coming through.
And don't worry.

409
00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:23.070
It's gonna be all
about Zach tonight.

410
00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:24.840
Zach!

411
00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:27.510
So we went out
to sushi on Wednesday.

412
00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:29.180
And we both ordered
the chicken teriyaki,

413
00:22:29.210 --> 00:22:31.050
which is like, "It's fate."

414
00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:33.480
And then I haven't heard
from him since, you know?

415
00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:35.480
Which is a bummer,
because I really liked him.

416
00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:36.950
He didn't laugh
at any of my jokes,

417
00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:39.190
but I felt like
there was something there.

418
00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:41.990
I don't know.
Not like I even care.

419
00:22:42.020 --> 00:22:45.190
It's like, whatever.
I should listen to my psychic.

420
00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:49.530
She says, "Stop dating losers,
and never go on a plane."

421
00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:50.600
I knew it.

422
00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:53.170
Oh, so you think
he's playing hard to get?

423
00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:55.870
Or the more likely scenario:

424
00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:57.870
He lost his phone in,
like, a fire.

425
00:22:57.910 --> 00:22:59.540
Yeah, I think he lost his phone.

426
00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:00.980
Yeah. I do too.

427
00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:03.440
You know, I... I totally forgot.

428
00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:06.080
I have a huge test on Monday
that I gotta study for.

429
00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:07.620
So I'm just gonna do that
all night,

430
00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:10.690
and definitely
don't come in my room.

431
00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:12.820
Oh, okay. Yeah. See you.

432
00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:14.520
Night, sweetie.

433
00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:17.690
But you know what?
I'm just gonna call him.

434
00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:19.730
Now I'm worried he's dead.

435
00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:27.700
Hey, hey, hey.

436
00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:29.840
Over here.

437
00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:31.470
Wait. So how is this gonna work?

438
00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:33.010
Are you my wingman,
or am I yours?

439
00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:34.840
Is that what you're wearing
to the dance?

440
00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:36.240
I gotta tell you something.
Get down.

441
00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:38.050
Dude, no. This is a new suit.
Get off.

442
00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:40.150
Where are the girls?
Uh, yeah, about that.

443
00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:41.880
I just said that
to get you over here.

444
00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:43.050
I need your help.

445
00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:44.620
So there are no girls?

446
00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:46.250
Well, there is one girl.

447
00:23:46.290 --> 00:23:47.590
Oh! My man!

448
00:23:47.620 --> 00:23:49.260
Shh! What? What?

449
00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:52.830
But she's locked in this house,
and her dad's a psychopath.

450
00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.860
Does she have a friend?

451
00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:57.200
No. I'm serious.

452
00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:01.100
You know, you said there was
gonna be girls,

453
00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.740
and not only are there no girls,

454
00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:04.970
but there's a psychopath,
and I'm in a suit.

455
00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:06.650
How do you know
this guy's going to leave?

456
00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:08.280
I called him and pretended
to be the cops.

457
00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:10.140
And I asked him to come
to the station.

458
00:24:10.180 --> 00:24:12.780
You can get in trouble for that.
It's just a written warning.

459
00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:15.920
Dude. It's wet dirt, dude.
My pants are gonna get muddied.

460
00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:17.750
He's right there.

461
00:24:23.320 --> 00:24:24.590
Whoa.

462
00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:35.140
All right. Let's go.

463
00:24:40.640 --> 00:24:41.780
Come on.

464
00:24:41.810 --> 00:24:43.310
Okay, okay.

465
00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:45.780
Dude, my dry-cleaning bill's
gonna be ridiculous.

466
00:24:45.810 --> 00:24:47.620
Just come on.

467
00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:55.220
Whoa. Where'd you learn that,
New York?

468
00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:57.330
No, YouTube. Oh.

469
00:25:04.100 --> 00:25:05.900
Okay, stay here
and watch the driveway.

470
00:25:05.930 --> 00:25:08.670
Wait here by myself?
Out in the dark?

471
00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:10.770
Yes, Champ. You're the lookout.

472
00:25:10.810 --> 00:25:13.040
If Shivers comes back,
you just give me a sign like:

473
00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:15.880
Okay, just so we're clear,

474
00:25:15.910 --> 00:25:19.680
if I sense any danger,
I will run the other way.

475
00:25:51.350 --> 00:25:52.380
Whoa!

476
00:25:56.950 --> 00:25:58.820
Where am I?

477
00:26:08.730 --> 00:26:11.230
What the hell? You're supposed
to be the lookout.

478
00:26:11.270 --> 00:26:12.800
And that's not gonna change.

479
00:26:12.830 --> 00:26:14.740
I'll just be the lookout,
you know, in here.

480
00:26:14.770 --> 00:26:18.240
No, no, by definition you have
to be somewhere out, looking.

481
00:26:18.270 --> 00:26:20.010
Let me explain something
to you, Zacharias.

482
00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:22.340
You know how they say
teenagers have no fear of death?

483
00:26:22.380 --> 00:26:24.910
That they're never gonna
get hurt? Well, not me, okay?

484
00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:27.280
I was born with the gift
of fear. I remember being 4,

485
00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:28.880
being pushed on a swing
and thinking,

486
00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:30.990
"This is how it ends."
You're not gonna die.

487
00:26:31.020 --> 00:26:32.750
All right? At least not today.

488
00:26:32.790 --> 00:26:34.160
Okay? It's gonna be okay.

489
00:26:34.190 --> 00:26:35.820
Yeah, you're right. Okay.

490
00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:37.690
I'm being ridiculous.

491
00:26:39.060 --> 00:26:41.160
Oh, bear traps.

492
00:26:43.400 --> 00:26:48.140
Who puts bear traps in their
basement? I mean, seriously.

493
00:26:51.210 --> 00:26:52.870
Let's go.

494
00:26:54.180 --> 00:26:56.880
Let's go outside
where it's safe.

495
00:26:56.910 --> 00:26:59.850
Where there's no bear traps.

496
00:27:09.820 --> 00:27:12.190
I think I swallowed some web.

497
00:27:24.370 --> 00:27:27.780
Dude, this way.
Come on. Come on.

498
00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:42.820
Up there.

499
00:27:42.860 --> 00:27:44.190
Oh...

500
00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:55.170
It's coming from that room.

501
00:27:57.340 --> 00:27:58.970
Hannah?

502
00:28:23.500 --> 00:28:26.170
That's weird.
It's like the noise

503
00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:28.200
is coming from this bookcase.

504
00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:30.240
Well, it's an old house.

505
00:28:32.040 --> 00:28:35.310
Whoa. Check this out.

506
00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:37.010
<i>The Scarecrow Walks at Midnight.</i>

507
00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:41.550
<i>The Ghost Next Door,
Night of the Living Dummy.</i>

508
00:28:41.580 --> 00:28:43.880
<i>These are all
Goosebumps manuscripts.</i>

509
00:28:43.920 --> 00:28:46.290
What's he doing with a bunch
of kids' books?

510
00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:48.290
These aren't kids' books. Okay?

511
00:28:48.320 --> 00:28:50.090
Kids' books help you
fall asleep.

512
00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:51.530
These books keep you up
all night.

513
00:28:51.560 --> 00:28:53.790
Okay. "R.L. Stine."

514
00:28:53.830 --> 00:28:55.560
Whatever happened to that guy?

515
00:28:55.600 --> 00:28:57.360
Uh, who knows?
He disappeared one day.

516
00:28:57.400 --> 00:28:58.800
Does it matter? Let's go.

517
00:28:58.830 --> 00:29:00.330
<i>The Abominable Snowman
of Pasadena.</i>

518
00:29:00.370 --> 00:29:02.170
My grandma lives in Pasadena.

519
00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:03.970
I stopped visiting
after reading this.

520
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:05.240
Okay.

521
00:29:05.270 --> 00:29:06.940
We're not here for book club.

522
00:29:06.970 --> 00:29:09.440
I know, but why
are these books locked?

523
00:29:09.480 --> 00:29:11.210
I mean, who would lock a book?

524
00:29:11.250 --> 00:29:13.450
Maybe there's like
a key or something

525
00:29:13.480 --> 00:29:15.280
we can unlock it with.

526
00:29:15.320 --> 00:29:20.020
Okay, if it really matters that
much, look at this. All right?

527
00:29:20.050 --> 00:29:21.260
Mystery solved.

528
00:29:21.290 --> 00:29:23.320
Let's get back to why...
Look out!

529
00:29:26.890 --> 00:29:28.030
Zach?

530
00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:30.830
Hey, Hannah.

531
00:29:30.870 --> 00:29:33.070
What are you doing in my house?

532
00:29:33.100 --> 00:29:36.400
I thought you were
chained up, possibly.

533
00:29:36.440 --> 00:29:38.540
Why did you think that?
Because I heard you scream,

534
00:29:38.570 --> 00:29:41.240
and then I called the... police.

535
00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:42.610
Okay, both of you
need to go right now.

536
00:29:42.640 --> 00:29:44.980
Yes. Okay.
Wait. One... One second.

537
00:29:45.010 --> 00:29:47.880
Hi. Hi, I'm Champ.
Nice to meet you.

538
00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:50.950
Hey, we're going to
the semiformal later tonight,

539
00:29:50.990 --> 00:29:55.590
and I don't know, you should
come and invite a friend.

540
00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:57.490
I really don't care
what she looks like.

541
00:29:57.530 --> 00:29:59.460
Did you unlock a book?

542
00:29:59.490 --> 00:30:01.860
Yeah. I did. I'm sorry.
It's around somewhere.

543
00:30:01.900 --> 00:30:04.060
I just dropped it. And I'll
put it back where it belongs

544
00:30:04.100 --> 00:30:06.070
and we'll be out of your hair.
Here it is...

545
00:30:06.100 --> 00:30:07.230
No! Don't open it!

546
00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:11.310
No!

547
00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:17.370
What's going on?
Nobody make a sound.

548
00:31:37.320 --> 00:31:38.560
My dad's gonna kill me.

549
00:31:43.160 --> 00:31:45.170
Wait! Zach!

550
00:31:45.200 --> 00:31:47.030
Zach!

551
00:31:57.240 --> 00:31:59.650
Wait, Hannah.

552
00:31:59.680 --> 00:32:01.680
Hannah. Hannah, wait.

553
00:32:01.720 --> 00:32:03.480
Go home, Zach.
You're in over your head.

554
00:32:03.520 --> 00:32:04.990
You wanna tell me
what's going on?

555
00:32:05.020 --> 00:32:06.550
No, I can't explain.
I have to go.

556
00:32:06.590 --> 00:32:08.420
Zach, wait. Wait.

557
00:32:08.460 --> 00:32:09.720
Come on. Listen.

558
00:32:09.760 --> 00:32:13.230
Stop. Stop. Stop.
Dude, what are you doing?

559
00:32:13.260 --> 00:32:14.700
Dude. Dude, get off me.

560
00:32:14.730 --> 00:32:17.500
Listen to me very carefully.
That's the Abominable Snowman.

561
00:32:17.530 --> 00:32:19.330
You don't get that nickname
by accident.

562
00:32:19.370 --> 00:32:20.630
And it just crawled
out of a book.

563
00:32:20.670 --> 00:32:22.300
That doesn't just happen, Zach!

564
00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:24.100
I'm going after Hannah.

565
00:32:24.140 --> 00:32:27.210
Look, I read what it did
to Pasadena.

566
00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:29.180
It's no joke, man.

567
00:32:49.230 --> 00:32:50.530
She went in there.

568
00:32:50.560 --> 00:32:52.730
Yeah. She's not the only one
who went in there.

569
00:33:00.070 --> 00:33:02.610
Dude, we should call the cops.

570
00:33:02.640 --> 00:33:05.550
Have you met the cops
in this town?

571
00:33:05.580 --> 00:33:07.480
Fair enough.

572
00:33:22.860 --> 00:33:25.770
Do you see the scratches
on that wall?

573
00:33:27.170 --> 00:33:28.700
Yes.

574
00:33:28.740 --> 00:33:31.270
Just making sure.

575
00:33:33.640 --> 00:33:36.380
Oh! Is that your scream?

576
00:33:36.410 --> 00:33:38.510
Don't judge me.

577
00:33:39.580 --> 00:33:41.220
Over here.

578
00:33:41.250 --> 00:33:42.780
This way.

579
00:33:50.690 --> 00:33:53.560
What is she gonna do,
read it a story?

580
00:34:08.910 --> 00:34:11.880
Hannah? What is happening?
How did that pop out of a book?

581
00:34:11.910 --> 00:34:14.550
Shh. It's in here.
Hey, we should get a gun.

582
00:34:14.580 --> 00:34:18.190
Are you kidding? We need a tank.

583
00:34:18.220 --> 00:34:21.320
Wait. He's made out of snow.

584
00:34:21.360 --> 00:34:22.490
Flamethrower. Bag of salt.

585
00:34:22.520 --> 00:34:24.190
Flamethrower. Quiet.

586
00:34:24.220 --> 00:34:26.190
He can't be killed.

587
00:34:39.440 --> 00:34:41.340
It's candy.

588
00:34:50.350 --> 00:34:51.620
Look out!

589
00:35:07.800 --> 00:35:10.500
Come on. It's distracted.

590
00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:13.210
- Hannah, come on. Let's go.
- No, what are you doing?

591
00:35:13.240 --> 00:35:15.280
Get off. No. Stop it!
No, you don't understand.

592
00:35:15.310 --> 00:35:17.540
The only way to stop them is
to suck them back into the book.

593
00:35:17.580 --> 00:35:19.850
Drop the book and let it
suck itself back in.

594
00:35:19.880 --> 00:35:21.920
No, I'm not close enough.

595
00:35:31.690 --> 00:35:33.430
What are you doing?
Just open the book.

596
00:35:33.460 --> 00:35:35.700
Just wait.

597
00:35:35.730 --> 00:35:37.870
- Hannah, open the book.
- Not yet.

598
00:35:37.900 --> 00:35:40.270
Hannah! Now!

599
00:35:43.370 --> 00:35:44.540
The book.

600
00:35:44.570 --> 00:35:45.710
Hannah, what are you doing?

601
00:35:45.740 --> 00:35:47.310
Hannah. Huh?

602
00:35:54.450 --> 00:35:56.650
No. No.

603
00:36:00.750 --> 00:36:02.360
Don't let it get the book!

604
00:36:12.570 --> 00:36:14.400
Are you okay? Yeah.

605
00:36:14.430 --> 00:36:16.900
Guys, come on, let's go!
Come on. Come on.

606
00:36:16.940 --> 00:36:19.270
Over here! Come on!

607
00:36:19.310 --> 00:36:21.710
- Come on.
- Good idea. Punch it.

608
00:36:25.050 --> 00:36:27.250
Bad idea. Bad idea.
Get off that thing.

609
00:36:27.280 --> 00:36:29.420
Aah!

610
00:36:55.540 --> 00:36:56.840
Run.

611
00:36:56.880 --> 00:37:00.850
Hurry, this way.
Guys, come on. In here.

612
00:37:00.880 --> 00:37:03.450
Guys, come on. Hurry!

613
00:37:16.830 --> 00:37:18.800
Yes.

614
00:37:28.580 --> 00:37:30.440
Whoa!

615
00:38:23.160 --> 00:38:27.030
All of you in the car, now!

616
00:38:28.500 --> 00:38:29.970
What are you gonna do to us?

617
00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:31.440
Silence.

618
00:38:31.470 --> 00:38:32.940
We can't ask questions...? Shut up!

619
00:38:32.970 --> 00:38:34.640
Dad, they were only
trying to help.

620
00:38:34.680 --> 00:38:37.380
I told you to stay away from us,
or something bad would happen.

621
00:38:37.410 --> 00:38:40.480
But that's the problem with kids
today. They don't listen.

622
00:38:40.510 --> 00:38:43.020
<i>You had to pick
Abominable Snowman of Pasadena.</i>

623
00:38:43.050 --> 00:38:45.950
<i>You couldn't have picked
Little Shop of Hamsters.</i>

624
00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:48.390
You're him, aren't you?

625
00:38:48.420 --> 00:38:50.790
Hm?

626
00:38:50.820 --> 00:38:53.760
- You're R.L. Stine.
- R.L. who?

627
00:38:53.790 --> 00:38:54.930
I don't know who that is.

628
00:38:54.960 --> 00:38:56.430
Oh, really?

629
00:38:57.900 --> 00:39:00.470
Well, just as well,
because his books suck.

630
00:39:01.770 --> 00:39:03.100
What are you doing?

631
00:39:03.140 --> 00:39:05.810
I can't decide
which one I hate more:

632
00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:07.870
<i>Monster Blood or Go Eat Worms!</i>

633
00:39:07.910 --> 00:39:09.810
I'm so confused.

634
00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:11.650
You see the endings coming
from a mile away.

635
00:39:11.680 --> 00:39:14.780
It's like stop trying to be
Stephen King, man.

636
00:39:19.120 --> 00:39:21.020
Let me tell you something
about Steve King.

637
00:39:21.050 --> 00:39:24.060
Steve King wishes
he could write like me,

638
00:39:24.090 --> 00:39:26.090
and I've sold
way more books than him,

639
00:39:26.130 --> 00:39:27.790
but nobody ever
talks about that!

640
00:39:27.830 --> 00:39:30.030
Okay. Way more books!

641
00:39:30.060 --> 00:39:31.970
Dad... Aah!

642
00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:35.570
Your face is doing
the red thing again.

643
00:39:35.600 --> 00:39:36.900
No way.

644
00:39:36.940 --> 00:39:39.670
Wait, you're R.L. Stine?
That's you?

645
00:39:39.710 --> 00:39:41.580
Really? Really?

646
00:39:41.610 --> 00:39:43.140
Hey, can I get a picture
real quick?

647
00:39:43.180 --> 00:39:44.780
No. No. Come on. Come on.

648
00:39:44.810 --> 00:39:46.210
The answer's "yes." I said no.

649
00:39:46.250 --> 00:39:49.420
What? I... No!
Get that thing out of here!

650
00:39:50.850 --> 00:39:53.790
I'm sorry. I just wanted a photo
real quick for my Instagram.

651
00:39:53.820 --> 00:39:55.190
Oh, is that all? Let me see.

652
00:39:55.220 --> 00:39:57.520
Oh, yeah. Here you go.
Thank you.

653
00:40:18.210 --> 00:40:19.580
Hey, hey, what happens now?

654
00:40:19.610 --> 00:40:20.980
You go home, put on your p.j.'s,

655
00:40:21.010 --> 00:40:22.650
get your blankie,
you go nap-nap.

656
00:40:22.680 --> 00:40:25.020
In the morning, this will
all just feel like a bad dream.

657
00:40:25.050 --> 00:40:27.120
Dad, wait.
There's no time. Start packing.

658
00:40:27.150 --> 00:40:29.220
We're moving again.

659
00:40:31.160 --> 00:40:35.030
So, what do you wanna do now?

660
00:40:35.060 --> 00:40:37.100
Zach, dude.

661
00:40:37.130 --> 00:40:39.930
- But I don't wanna leave.
- I like it here.

662
00:40:39.970 --> 00:40:41.740
Hannah, you have to understand.

663
00:40:41.770 --> 00:40:43.900
I don't have to understand
anything.

664
00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:45.640
Why can't we be normal for once?

665
00:40:45.670 --> 00:40:48.540
Because we're not a normal
family. Now go get your things.

666
00:40:48.580 --> 00:40:49.740
I'm so over this.

667
00:40:49.780 --> 00:40:52.580
Oh! Teenagers.

668
00:41:03.790 --> 00:41:05.830
I could've killed you.

669
00:41:05.860 --> 00:41:09.260
That was a terrible throw. How?

670
00:41:09.300 --> 00:41:10.960
What are you doing here?
Go home.

671
00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:13.170
No. Not until you explain
what's going on.

672
00:41:13.200 --> 00:41:15.100
No, no, no. I can't explain it.

673
00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:17.570
We were almost just eaten
by Frosty the Snowman,

674
00:41:17.600 --> 00:41:19.770
which should be impossible,
by the way, so try.

675
00:41:19.810 --> 00:41:22.310
Okay, look...

676
00:41:23.610 --> 00:41:25.710
Where do I begin? When I was
younger,

677
00:41:25.750 --> 00:41:28.180
I suffered from terrible
allergies that kept me indoors.

678
00:41:28.220 --> 00:41:31.650
And all the kids
threw rocks at my window

679
00:41:31.690 --> 00:41:33.820
and called me names.

680
00:41:33.850 --> 00:41:35.790
So I created my own friends.

681
00:41:35.820 --> 00:41:40.630
Monsters, demons, ghouls
to terrorize my neighborhood

682
00:41:40.660 --> 00:41:42.330
and all the kids
that made fun of me.

683
00:41:42.360 --> 00:41:46.070
And they became real to me.

684
00:41:46.100 --> 00:41:49.770
And then one day,
they actually...

685
00:41:49.800 --> 00:41:54.310
became real.

686
00:41:57.240 --> 00:42:00.310
My monsters literally
leapt off the page.

687
00:42:00.350 --> 00:42:02.950
As long as the books
remain locked, we're safe.

688
00:42:02.980 --> 00:42:05.220
But when they open,

689
00:42:05.250 --> 00:42:10.060
well, you've just seen
what happens.

690
00:42:10.090 --> 00:42:12.790
I'm allergic to dust mites.

691
00:42:12.830 --> 00:42:14.690
What's your point?

692
00:42:14.730 --> 00:42:16.660
I'm just saying,
I have allergies too.

693
00:42:16.700 --> 00:42:18.200
So I understand.

694
00:42:20.230 --> 00:42:23.700
Why am I talking to you?
Hannah, let's go.

695
00:42:26.740 --> 00:42:28.740
Hannah! I'm sorry.

696
00:42:31.780 --> 00:42:33.250
Let's go.

697
00:42:35.180 --> 00:42:36.880
Hannah, you grab A to M,
I'll get M to Z.

698
00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:39.850
And keep the man-eating plant
away from the bug-eyed aliens.

699
00:42:39.890 --> 00:42:42.120
Oh, no. Not him.

700
00:42:42.160 --> 00:42:45.190
Hello, Papa.

701
00:42:49.060 --> 00:42:51.930
How long's it been?

702
00:42:51.970 --> 00:42:53.630
Feels like forever.

703
00:42:55.000 --> 00:42:56.640
Who are your new friends?

704
00:42:56.670 --> 00:42:58.640
We're not friends.
Barely know him.

705
00:42:58.670 --> 00:43:01.170
Slappy, it's so nice
to see you again.

706
00:43:01.210 --> 00:43:03.110
Did you miss me?

707
00:43:03.140 --> 00:43:04.880
Of course I missed you.

708
00:43:08.850 --> 00:43:11.280
So, what's the plan, friend?

709
00:43:11.320 --> 00:43:13.720
You must've brought me out
for something fun.

710
00:43:13.750 --> 00:43:16.820
Terrorize the locals?
Destroy the town?

711
00:43:16.860 --> 00:43:18.930
Let's get silly.

712
00:43:18.960 --> 00:43:20.260
You guessed it, Slappy.

713
00:43:20.290 --> 00:43:23.060
I'm going to destroy Madison,
and I...

714
00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:25.200
And I couldn't do it
without you.

715
00:43:25.230 --> 00:43:28.100
Aw, shucks. You're giving me...

716
00:43:28.130 --> 00:43:30.440
Oh, what's the word?

717
00:43:30.470 --> 00:43:32.440
Goosebumps.

718
00:43:33.910 --> 00:43:35.880
Oh, my God. He's so creepy.

719
00:43:35.910 --> 00:43:37.980
Oh, he is such a crack-up.

720
00:43:38.010 --> 00:43:40.310
Such a clever dummy.

721
00:43:40.350 --> 00:43:44.150
Who are you calling "dummy,"
dummy?

722
00:43:48.790 --> 00:43:50.790
You're trying to put me back in?

723
00:43:50.820 --> 00:43:53.330
No, no, no, no, no, no.
Don't be silly.

724
00:43:53.360 --> 00:43:56.060
I know when you're lying to me,
Papa.

725
00:43:59.230 --> 00:44:02.340
You've made Slappy very unhappy.

726
00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:06.740
He's not going back on the shelf
ever again.

727
00:44:06.770 --> 00:44:08.170
Slappy, no, wait!

728
00:44:10.010 --> 00:44:11.780
I think it's time I started

729
00:44:11.810 --> 00:44:14.280
pulling the strings
in this relationship.

730
00:44:14.310 --> 00:44:18.280
Tonight is gonna be the best
story you've ever written.

731
00:44:18.320 --> 00:44:22.120
All of your children
are coming out to play.

732
00:44:25.290 --> 00:44:27.830
Oh, thank God he's gone.

733
00:44:27.860 --> 00:44:30.300
Oh, God. He's gone.

734
00:44:32.200 --> 00:44:34.170
And he's taken all the books.

735
00:44:46.050 --> 00:44:48.920
That one's a real page-turner.

736
00:44:57.090 --> 00:44:59.530
<i>Congratulations.
You've just released a demon.</i>

737
00:44:59.560 --> 00:45:03.000
A ventriloquist dummy with
a serious Napoleonic complex.

738
00:45:03.030 --> 00:45:05.200
I only opened one book, and now
I see that was a mistake.

739
00:45:05.230 --> 00:45:07.870
The snowman must've knocked
Slappy's book down.

740
00:45:07.900 --> 00:45:10.100
- I still blame him.
- I don't like you, boy.

741
00:45:11.500 --> 00:45:13.340
It's locked from the outside.

742
00:45:15.580 --> 00:45:18.950
Out the kitchen door. Go now.

743
00:45:24.950 --> 00:45:27.220
Why is that here? I don't know.

744
00:46:00.520 --> 00:46:03.420
Maybe they're friendly.

745
00:46:04.560 --> 00:46:07.260
Not friendly.
Definitely not friendly.

746
00:46:07.290 --> 00:46:09.000
Ooh.

747
00:46:17.540 --> 00:46:19.270
He's stuck to my face.

748
00:46:19.310 --> 00:46:21.470
Definitely not friendly.

749
00:46:21.510 --> 00:46:23.040
Dad! Aah!

750
00:46:24.940 --> 00:46:26.350
Hold on. I'll save you.

751
00:46:28.580 --> 00:46:30.920
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
Are you okay?

752
00:46:38.160 --> 00:46:40.490
Ready, set, go.

753
00:46:46.130 --> 00:46:47.570
I'm sorry.

754
00:46:49.400 --> 00:46:51.970
Help me. Oh, no, no, no.
Help, someone.

755
00:46:52.010 --> 00:46:53.370
Get back. Get back.

756
00:46:58.410 --> 00:46:59.910
Get back.

757
00:46:59.950 --> 00:47:02.150
Heave-ho. Heave-ho.

758
00:47:02.180 --> 00:47:03.450
Heave-ho.

759
00:47:04.680 --> 00:47:06.650
Help me. Help me. Get them off.
Okay, okay.

760
00:47:06.690 --> 00:47:08.960
Heave-ho. Heave-ho.

761
00:47:08.990 --> 00:47:10.420
Quickly.

762
00:47:11.420 --> 00:47:13.160
Shut it. Shut it.

763
00:47:13.190 --> 00:47:16.930
- Did you get them all?
- Heave-ho. Heave-ho...

764
00:47:16.960 --> 00:47:17.960
Untie me.

765
00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:19.600
I imagined something different.

766
00:47:19.630 --> 00:47:21.500
"Come over to my house.
There will be girls.

767
00:47:21.530 --> 00:47:23.140
I'm your wingman."

768
00:47:32.450 --> 00:47:34.350
Oh, no, no, no.
We got to get out of here.

769
00:47:34.380 --> 00:47:35.550
We need to get to the basement.

770
00:47:35.580 --> 00:47:38.320
It's locked. I picked it.

771
00:47:38.350 --> 00:47:40.290
That's breaking and entering!

772
00:47:42.320 --> 00:47:44.520
Watch out for the bear traps.

773
00:47:47.590 --> 00:47:49.160
Why'd it have to be bear traps?

774
00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:52.170
- All right, come on. Hurry.
- Come on.

775
00:48:06.610 --> 00:48:10.550
- Lock it! Lock it!
- Okay.

776
00:48:10.580 --> 00:48:12.550
Why couldn't you have
written stories

777
00:48:12.590 --> 00:48:14.590
about rainbows and unicorns?

778
00:48:14.620 --> 00:48:17.160
Because that doesn't sell
400 million copies.

779
00:48:17.190 --> 00:48:18.420
Whoa, domestic?

780
00:48:18.460 --> 00:48:20.060
No, worldwide.

781
00:48:20.090 --> 00:48:22.530
It's still very impressive.
Shut up.

782
00:48:31.100 --> 00:48:32.410
What is that?

783
00:48:53.790 --> 00:48:56.100
He's burning the books.
Why's he doing that?

784
00:48:56.130 --> 00:48:58.630
So there's no way to get
the monsters back inside.

785
00:48:58.670 --> 00:49:02.100
It's Slappy's revenge.

786
00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:05.570
<i>Slappy's Revenge.
That's a good title.</i>

787
00:49:11.640 --> 00:49:13.480
Sorry, folks. I'd slow down,

788
00:49:13.510 --> 00:49:15.450
but I can't reach the brake.

789
00:49:18.790 --> 00:49:22.160
Hey, check out
my new best seller.

790
00:49:22.190 --> 00:49:24.720
It'll grow on you.

791
00:49:31.160 --> 00:49:35.130
Dropped calls are gonna be the
least of this town's problems.

792
00:49:36.470 --> 00:49:39.810
I'm driving myself crazy!

793
00:49:53.520 --> 00:49:56.460
- The town has been invaded.
- Communications are down.

794
00:49:56.490 --> 00:50:01.430
We're talking mass chaos,
and no one knows how to stop it.

795
00:50:01.460 --> 00:50:02.830
What do you think?

796
00:50:02.860 --> 00:50:05.570
I'm not sure. I...
I'm not... I don't know.

797
00:50:05.600 --> 00:50:08.170
<i>It's The Blob.</i>

798
00:50:08.200 --> 00:50:10.570
<i>The Blob.
The original one with Steve McQueen.</i>

799
00:50:10.600 --> 00:50:13.570
Oh, I can't believe
you don't know that movie.

800
00:50:13.610 --> 00:50:15.810
Come over to my house.
I got it on LaserDisc.

801
00:50:15.840 --> 00:50:17.140
We'll wa...

802
00:50:18.480 --> 00:50:20.750
Power went out again.

803
00:50:20.780 --> 00:50:23.850
God. All night with this.

804
00:50:23.880 --> 00:50:27.150
Well, these emergency lights
should kick on soon.

805
00:50:35.560 --> 00:50:38.200
Somebody left
their ventriloquist dummy.

806
00:50:40.200 --> 00:50:42.600
Who you calling "dummy"?

807
00:50:42.640 --> 00:50:45.570
It's talking.
What is that thing?

808
00:50:45.610 --> 00:50:48.270
I come in peace. Unarmed.

809
00:50:48.310 --> 00:50:51.140
I just wanna read you
a bedtime story.

810
00:50:51.180 --> 00:50:52.680
- Sir, shut your mouth.
- Okay.

811
00:50:52.710 --> 00:50:54.350
Because that's not gonna
stop me.

812
00:50:54.380 --> 00:50:56.150
Hands where I can see them.
Officers!

813
00:50:56.180 --> 00:51:00.190
You've been relieved
of your duties. Ha, ha!

814
00:51:00.220 --> 00:51:02.260
Now, freeze.

815
00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:13.530
Hello?

816
00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:21.240
Oh, hello, cutie.
You must be lost.

817
00:51:22.410 --> 00:51:23.780
Oh, and no tags.

818
00:51:23.810 --> 00:51:25.310
Well, let's get you some water.

819
00:51:25.340 --> 00:51:27.180
We'll take you around
the neighborhood

820
00:51:27.210 --> 00:51:28.850
and we'll find your owner.

821
00:51:28.880 --> 00:51:31.880
Is he handsome? Is he single?

822
00:51:31.920 --> 00:51:35.520
Is he thinking about leaving
his wife and needs a push?

823
00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:44.460
All right. Trying not to spill.

824
00:51:44.500 --> 00:51:46.500
Don't be clumsy, Lorraine.

825
00:51:46.530 --> 00:51:49.840
Okay, you must be so thirsty.

826
00:52:19.630 --> 00:52:21.700
Everyone in town's been frozen.

827
00:52:31.810 --> 00:52:35.210
Oh, my God. Oh, my God, Dad.
Dad, what happened to...?

828
00:52:37.350 --> 00:52:38.480
Wait.

829
00:52:38.520 --> 00:52:40.690
Oh. Oh, thank God.

830
00:52:40.720 --> 00:52:42.990
Guys, false alarm.
It's not my dad.

831
00:52:44.620 --> 00:52:45.760
What are we going to do?

832
00:52:45.790 --> 00:52:46.930
Without those manuscripts,

833
00:52:46.960 --> 00:52:48.830
there's nothing I can do.

834
00:52:50.360 --> 00:52:52.330
If... If you wrote the monsters
off the page,

835
00:52:52.370 --> 00:52:54.500
then maybe there's a way
you could write them back on.

836
00:52:54.530 --> 00:52:56.640
Wait... Yeah, yeah, yeah!
Why don't you just do that?

837
00:52:56.670 --> 00:52:58.910
You have any idea how many
stories I'd have to write

838
00:52:58.940 --> 00:53:00.740
to capture every monster
I've created?

839
00:53:00.770 --> 00:53:02.480
I already have carpal tunnel
in both hands.

840
00:53:02.510 --> 00:53:04.740
Dad, just listen to him.
It's a great idea.

841
00:53:04.780 --> 00:53:08.280
Just one.
One story to capture them all.

842
00:53:08.310 --> 00:53:10.680
Hmm, simple.
Just one, one story,

843
00:53:10.720 --> 00:53:12.820
with every monster
I've ever created.

844
00:53:12.850 --> 00:53:17.590
Brilliant. Really good idea.
He's a keeper.

845
00:53:17.620 --> 00:53:18.760
You have a better idea?

846
00:53:18.790 --> 00:53:19.890
Mm-hm, mm-hm.

847
00:53:19.930 --> 00:53:21.990
A much better idea.

848
00:53:23.700 --> 00:53:25.900
No, not now, I don't, but...

849
00:53:25.930 --> 00:53:27.730
Okay, then we gotta
get you to a computer

850
00:53:27.770 --> 00:53:29.270
so you can start writing.
There's...

851
00:53:29.300 --> 00:53:31.900
There's a computer store.
Just break in.

852
00:53:31.940 --> 00:53:34.740
No, no, no.
I need my typewriter.

853
00:53:34.770 --> 00:53:36.880
- What?
- Every story I've written

854
00:53:36.910 --> 00:53:39.910
was on that Smith Corona.
It's not just me.

855
00:53:39.950 --> 00:53:43.780
That typewriter is special.

856
00:53:43.820 --> 00:53:46.920
It has a soul of its own.

857
00:53:46.950 --> 00:53:49.660
If I write on anything else,
it won't work.

858
00:53:49.690 --> 00:53:51.320
Where's the typewriter?

859
00:53:51.360 --> 00:53:53.590
Oh, don't worry.

860
00:53:53.630 --> 00:53:55.960
It's somewhere safe.

861
00:53:58.400 --> 00:54:00.430
<i>? Get ugly</i>

862
00:54:01.570 --> 00:54:03.670
<i>? And everybody say</i>

863
00:54:03.700 --> 00:54:05.500
<i>? Get ugly</i>

864
00:54:07.870 --> 00:54:09.910
<i>? Get ugly</i>

865
00:54:09.940 --> 00:54:11.410
<i>? Get ugly.</i>

866
00:54:11.440 --> 00:54:13.550
Come on.

867
00:54:13.580 --> 00:54:15.580
Come on, come on, come on.

868
00:54:19.450 --> 00:54:20.920
Just give me one bar.

869
00:54:23.590 --> 00:54:26.360
This was working earlier.

870
00:54:26.390 --> 00:54:28.090
Brains. Aah!

871
00:54:28.130 --> 00:54:30.900
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to scare you.

872
00:54:30.930 --> 00:54:33.000
I mean, I did mean to scare you,
but in a playful way.

873
00:54:33.030 --> 00:54:36.070
So, uh, is everything okay?

874
00:54:37.570 --> 00:54:40.040
I'm sorry, I have to get hold
of my son,

875
00:54:40.070 --> 00:54:41.810
and I can't get any service.

876
00:54:41.840 --> 00:54:44.380
Yeah. No one can tonight.
It's weird.

877
00:54:47.880 --> 00:54:50.880
I don't know what's going
on with my phone.

878
00:54:50.920 --> 00:54:52.520
I can't get reception.

879
00:54:52.550 --> 00:54:54.590
Slappy's taken out
the cell-phone towers.

880
00:54:54.620 --> 00:54:56.790
That's what I'd do.

881
00:54:56.820 --> 00:54:59.030
He's cutting us off.
Isolating us.

882
00:54:59.060 --> 00:55:02.560
What was that?

883
00:55:04.660 --> 00:55:07.500
Ugh, it's the Invisible Boy.
He's a menace.

884
00:55:09.670 --> 00:55:11.500
Ow!

885
00:55:11.540 --> 00:55:13.470
Shove him out the window.

886
00:55:13.510 --> 00:55:14.770
Roll up the window.

887
00:55:14.810 --> 00:55:17.010
He's got his tie! Help, help!

888
00:55:17.040 --> 00:55:18.610
Hold on.

889
00:55:20.680 --> 00:55:22.480
Not cool!

890
00:55:22.520 --> 00:55:23.680
Are you okay?

891
00:55:23.720 --> 00:55:25.050
Yeah. For sure.

892
00:55:26.490 --> 00:55:28.750
Yeah. Wait. Wait, look out!

893
00:55:37.960 --> 00:55:39.700
Are you okay? Yeah.

894
00:55:39.730 --> 00:55:41.030
Everyone okay?

895
00:55:41.070 --> 00:55:43.500
It came out of nowhere.

896
00:55:59.720 --> 00:56:02.920
I don't remember writing
about a giant praying mantis.

897
00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:06.060
Right. Now I remember.

898
00:56:06.090 --> 00:56:09.200
Get us out of here!

899
00:56:09.230 --> 00:56:12.100
What are you doing?
I can't drive if I can't see.

900
00:56:12.130 --> 00:56:14.070
Just go!

901
00:56:26.750 --> 00:56:28.750
Oh, my God!

902
00:56:28.780 --> 00:56:30.080
Watch out! Turn left!

903
00:56:30.120 --> 00:56:31.680
Stop driving straight!

904
00:56:31.720 --> 00:56:33.750
- He's catching up! Turn right!
- Step on it!

905
00:56:33.790 --> 00:56:36.990
Does someone else wanna drive?
I'll pull over right now.

906
00:57:29.210 --> 00:57:31.910
Why'd you come up
with something so freaky?

907
00:57:31.940 --> 00:57:33.910
I just have a knack for it,
I guess.

908
00:57:35.180 --> 00:57:37.480
Oh, no. My Wagoneer.

909
00:57:38.880 --> 00:57:40.890
I had such low mileage on it.

910
00:57:40.920 --> 00:57:42.590
How far are we
from the high school?

911
00:57:42.620 --> 00:57:43.990
Not too far.

912
00:57:44.020 --> 00:57:45.620
We can cut through the cemetery.

913
00:57:45.660 --> 00:57:46.860
I'm sorry, a cemetery?

914
00:57:46.890 --> 00:57:49.130
God, relax. The high school's
just past the woods.

915
00:57:49.160 --> 00:57:50.800
Wait, how do you know that?

916
00:57:50.830 --> 00:57:54.300
Uh, sometimes I get a little
stir-crazy and go exploring.

917
00:57:54.330 --> 00:57:56.970
When?
At night after you go to bed.

918
00:57:57.000 --> 00:57:59.610
You're grounded.
That is so unfair.

919
00:57:59.640 --> 00:58:02.010
No, it's fair.
You're bringing up good points,

920
00:58:02.040 --> 00:58:03.740
but let's keep moving
while you argue.

921
00:58:03.780 --> 00:58:06.750
Sneaking off in the middle
of the night with strange boys.

922
00:58:06.780 --> 00:58:10.050
Unbelievable. Shut it.

923
00:58:13.350 --> 00:58:15.250
Hey, hey, do you have a dollar
I could borrow?

924
00:58:15.290 --> 00:58:18.060
What? No. Why? I'm parched.

925
00:58:18.090 --> 00:58:20.330
Well, just take one.
I'm sure they'll understand.

926
00:58:20.360 --> 00:58:21.860
Really? Ha!

927
00:58:21.890 --> 00:58:25.030
Lemonade, grape or strawberry?

928
00:58:25.060 --> 00:58:27.930
Good God, man. Here. Orange.

929
00:58:29.170 --> 00:58:31.100
I don't know what
I was thinking.

930
00:58:31.140 --> 00:58:33.340
There is way more going on here
than New York.

931
00:58:33.370 --> 00:58:35.670
What? Uh, you cut yourself.

932
00:58:35.710 --> 00:58:38.880
Is it bad?
Uh, yeah. It's really bad.

933
00:58:38.910 --> 00:58:40.810
Is my face messed up?

934
00:58:40.850 --> 00:58:43.950
Yeah. Big time.

935
00:58:43.980 --> 00:58:45.780
You look exactly the same.

936
00:58:51.890 --> 00:58:53.230
Did you hear that?

937
00:59:53.790 --> 00:59:55.090
What are you doing?

938
00:59:55.120 --> 00:59:56.890
That's the Werewolf
of Fever Swamp.

939
00:59:56.920 --> 00:59:59.120
He can smell my scent.

940
01:00:06.130 --> 01:00:08.270
No, it's not working.
I have to hide.

941
01:00:16.080 --> 01:00:17.880
Come on.

942
01:00:44.370 --> 01:00:47.110
Shh, no, no, no.

943
01:00:50.110 --> 01:00:52.210
Do something.

944
01:01:10.060 --> 01:01:11.200
Come on, come on. Come on.

945
01:01:15.270 --> 01:01:17.740
Come on. Go, go, go.

946
01:01:20.240 --> 01:01:23.180
He's on our tail. Go.

947
01:01:24.280 --> 01:01:26.810
Go! He's right behind us!

948
01:01:31.120 --> 01:01:32.950
Come on. Go, go.

949
01:01:32.990 --> 01:01:35.220
Oh!

950
01:01:36.220 --> 01:01:38.390
I'm stuck. Help me get out.

951
01:01:38.420 --> 01:01:40.930
What are you doing?
There's no time!

952
01:01:40.960 --> 01:01:44.030
I said get me out of here.
Gotta go. There's no time.

953
01:01:44.060 --> 01:01:47.100
I said get me out... Oh, no.
Keep going. He's chasing us.

954
01:01:47.130 --> 01:01:48.870
I'm going as fast as I can.

955
01:01:51.440 --> 01:01:54.470
Just go. We're right behind you.
Okay!

956
01:01:56.980 --> 01:01:58.880
Aah! Oh!

957
01:01:58.910 --> 01:02:01.180
Come on. We gotta go.
Get up. Get up.

958
01:02:01.210 --> 01:02:02.550
Come on, come on!
Let's go, guys!

959
01:02:02.580 --> 01:02:05.180
Come on, come on, come on.

960
01:02:06.290 --> 01:02:10.020
Ha! Let's see him
get through that.

961
01:02:12.220 --> 01:02:14.530
Go, go! Run, run!

962
01:02:28.540 --> 01:02:31.910
- It's locked.
- This way.

963
01:02:45.620 --> 01:02:48.360
I'm okay.

964
01:02:48.390 --> 01:02:50.500
I'm still okay!

965
01:02:50.530 --> 01:02:52.560
Who is that?
It's my Aunt Lorraine.

966
01:02:54.030 --> 01:02:55.200
Oh, my gosh.

967
01:02:55.230 --> 01:02:56.570
I think I killed that bear.

968
01:02:56.600 --> 01:02:58.240
It was actually a werewolf.
What?

969
01:02:58.270 --> 01:03:00.070
Aunt Lorraine,
what are you doing here?

970
01:03:00.110 --> 01:03:03.180
This is the back of my store.
I didn't know where else to go.

971
01:03:03.210 --> 01:03:07.280
I can't get ahold of your mother
or the cops or anyone...

972
01:03:07.310 --> 01:03:09.550
Hello. Uh, hi. Hello.

973
01:03:09.580 --> 01:03:13.520
Hi. I don't think we've been
properly introduced.

974
01:03:13.550 --> 01:03:16.220
Um... I'm... I'm Lorraine.

975
01:03:16.260 --> 01:03:17.960
Hello. R.L. Stine.

976
01:03:17.990 --> 01:03:20.330
We owe you a great debt
of gratitude.

977
01:03:20.360 --> 01:03:22.260
Your reckless driving
saved our lives.

978
01:03:22.290 --> 01:03:23.930
Oh, that old thing?

979
01:03:25.130 --> 01:03:26.430
Lorraine. Lorraine.

980
01:03:26.470 --> 01:03:28.100
So... Lorraine.

981
01:03:28.130 --> 01:03:30.300
We don't have time.
I need you to go to the police

982
01:03:30.340 --> 01:03:32.040
and tell them to meet us
at the high school.

983
01:03:32.070 --> 01:03:34.470
All right? Can you do that?
I can do that. Okay.

984
01:03:34.510 --> 01:03:36.340
Oh, did you wanna
exchange numbers?

985
01:03:36.380 --> 01:03:38.410
It's not a good time, but yes!

986
01:03:47.650 --> 01:03:49.920
Oh, God, this is a bad idea.

987
01:03:49.960 --> 01:03:52.020
What was that?

988
01:04:01.400 --> 01:04:03.270
You okay? Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

989
01:04:03.300 --> 01:04:05.640
Yeah. Just a root.
Nothing scary here.

990
01:04:05.670 --> 01:04:08.140
So how did you get
the nickname "Champ"?

991
01:04:08.170 --> 01:04:09.910
It's not a nickname.

992
01:04:09.940 --> 01:04:12.640
Wait. That's your real name?
Is it short for something?

993
01:04:12.680 --> 01:04:14.580
My full name is Champion.

994
01:04:14.610 --> 01:04:17.520
Your actual name is Champion.

995
01:04:18.950 --> 01:04:20.190
Sorry.

996
01:04:20.220 --> 01:04:21.520
My dad won a bronze

997
01:04:21.550 --> 01:04:24.190
- back in the '92 Olympics.
- Really?

998
01:04:26.160 --> 01:04:28.660
My mom, she was
an all-American sprinter

999
01:04:28.690 --> 01:04:31.200
and a two-time
world debate champion.

1000
01:04:31.230 --> 01:04:34.030
So they named me "Champ."

1001
01:04:36.200 --> 01:04:39.170
Hey, you know, if you're scared,
I can hold your hand.

1002
01:04:39.200 --> 01:04:41.470
Please, you're the scaredy-cat.

1003
01:04:43.310 --> 01:04:45.580
Wait, wait. Hold on.
It's okay. It's just a statue.

1004
01:04:45.610 --> 01:04:46.950
All right? You're fine.

1005
01:04:46.980 --> 01:04:49.950
It's all right. All right?

1006
01:04:49.980 --> 01:04:53.050
Just give me a sec. It's...

1007
01:04:53.090 --> 01:04:55.990
It's caught on your jacket.

1008
01:04:56.020 --> 01:04:57.390
My hero.

1009
01:05:00.590 --> 01:05:04.200
There. You're free to go.

1010
01:05:23.250 --> 01:05:25.550
What is it?

1011
01:05:27.250 --> 01:05:28.550
Nothing.

1012
01:05:28.590 --> 01:05:30.990
Are you sure?

1013
01:05:34.390 --> 01:05:36.130
Yeah.

1014
01:05:36.160 --> 01:05:38.330
Yeah, totally. I'm fi...

1015
01:05:41.400 --> 01:05:43.400
Zach!

1016
01:05:52.140 --> 01:05:54.010
Run!

1017
01:05:54.050 --> 01:05:56.210
Ghouls. Go, go.

1018
01:06:03.190 --> 01:06:07.230
Oh, they're getting closer!

1019
01:06:07.260 --> 01:06:09.800
Go. Here. Go. Go.
Come on. Come on. Go, go, go.

1020
01:06:09.830 --> 01:06:12.530
Hurry, quick, quick, quick.

1021
01:06:12.560 --> 01:06:14.230
I'm stuck.

1022
01:06:14.270 --> 01:06:16.540
Go on without me. Save yourself.
Okay. Good luck.

1023
01:06:16.570 --> 01:06:20.210
No, I didn't mean it, Champion!

1024
01:06:20.240 --> 01:06:22.540
What kind of monster
would take me up on that offer?

1025
01:06:22.570 --> 01:06:26.240
Pull. Everybody pull.

1026
01:06:26.280 --> 01:06:29.610
I'll kill him.
Where is that little imbecile?

1027
01:06:31.580 --> 01:06:33.790
Wait for us, you coward!

1028
01:06:33.820 --> 01:06:36.620
All right. Okay, Lorraine.
You got this.

1029
01:06:36.660 --> 01:06:38.560
Just tell the cops to head
to the high school

1030
01:06:38.590 --> 01:06:40.460
and that everyone's in trouble.

1031
01:06:40.490 --> 01:06:42.330
You can do this. Okay.

1032
01:06:42.360 --> 01:06:44.660
Oh! Nope. Wrong door.

1033
01:06:46.800 --> 01:06:48.600
Hello?

1034
01:06:49.740 --> 01:06:52.300
Is anyone in here?

1035
01:06:54.170 --> 01:06:57.140
Calling all cops,
calling all the cops.

1036
01:06:57.180 --> 01:06:59.380
Head to the high school.
My nephew's in trouble.

1037
01:06:59.410 --> 01:07:00.680
He's with R.L. Stine.

1038
01:07:00.710 --> 01:07:02.750
They think they know
how to stop all this.

1039
01:07:02.780 --> 01:07:05.420
Hello? Can anyone hear me?

1040
01:07:05.450 --> 01:07:08.720
I can hear you.

1041
01:07:08.750 --> 01:07:12.460
Sergeant Slappy,
ready to protect and serve.

1042
01:07:12.490 --> 01:07:14.830
Oh, my goodness.

1043
01:07:14.860 --> 01:07:16.460
You're... Don't do it.

1044
01:07:16.500 --> 01:07:18.330
A talking... Don't say it.

1045
01:07:18.360 --> 01:07:20.830
Dummy. You said it.

1046
01:07:26.240 --> 01:07:30.140
You have the right
to remain silent.

1047
01:07:30.180 --> 01:07:31.740
Where did they put
my typewriter?

1048
01:07:31.780 --> 01:07:34.580
I know it was this way.
It might've been the other way.

1049
01:07:34.610 --> 01:07:36.150
- We should split up.
- What? No.

1050
01:07:36.180 --> 01:07:37.750
Have you ever read
one of your books?

1051
01:07:37.780 --> 01:07:39.250
We're never supposed
to split up.

1052
01:07:39.280 --> 01:07:43.260
Come on. How many display cases
could there be?

1053
01:07:43.290 --> 01:07:47.790
You're touching me.
Yeah. Hang on a second.

1054
01:07:47.830 --> 01:07:50.360
Hannah doesn't know, does she?
She doesn't know what?

1055
01:07:50.400 --> 01:07:52.730
That she's not real.

1056
01:07:55.900 --> 01:07:57.740
She thinks she's a person, okay?

1057
01:07:57.770 --> 01:07:59.840
Not just some figment
of your imagination.

1058
01:07:59.870 --> 01:08:01.540
How could... How could you
lie to her?

1059
01:08:01.570 --> 01:08:02.870
I was trying to protect her!

1060
01:08:02.910 --> 01:08:05.840
Oh, yeah?
Well, good job with that.

1061
01:08:05.880 --> 01:08:07.810
This gift of mine is a curse.

1062
01:08:07.850 --> 01:08:11.520
You have no idea how lonely
it's been until Hannah.

1063
01:08:11.550 --> 01:08:13.820
She's different.

1064
01:08:13.850 --> 01:08:16.350
I wrote her in such a way
that she thinks she's real,

1065
01:08:16.390 --> 01:08:19.760
and she is real to me, Zach.

1066
01:08:22.460 --> 01:08:25.230
I don't expect you
to understand.

1067
01:08:26.770 --> 01:08:29.230
Actually, I do.

1068
01:08:32.840 --> 01:08:35.240
I'm afraid of losing her.

1069
01:08:37.880 --> 01:08:40.410
And the truth is,
I'm afraid of being alone.

1070
01:08:40.450 --> 01:08:42.680
I suppose I stopped connecting
with real people

1071
01:08:42.710 --> 01:08:44.850
when I was your age.

1072
01:08:47.720 --> 01:08:51.390
After my dad died,
I shut everyone out too.

1073
01:08:52.790 --> 01:08:56.460
Maybe we can both start over,

1074
01:08:56.500 --> 01:08:58.860
if we're alive tomorrow.

1075
01:09:01.300 --> 01:09:04.970
There you are. Are you okay?

1076
01:09:05.000 --> 01:09:08.410
You look like
you just saw a ghost.

1077
01:09:08.440 --> 01:09:11.740
Okay. Well, come on.
We found the typewriter.

1078
01:09:14.450 --> 01:09:18.380
Oh, my sweet darling,
I've missed you so much. Mwah.

1079
01:09:19.780 --> 01:09:21.450
All right, so start writing.

1080
01:09:21.490 --> 01:09:23.860
Yes, but what's the story?

1081
01:09:23.890 --> 01:09:26.660
What do you mean? Monsters lose,
good guys win, the end.

1082
01:09:26.690 --> 01:09:28.230
No, no, no. It doesn't work

1083
01:09:28.260 --> 01:09:29.830
<i>unless it's a real
Goosebumps story,</i>

1084
01:09:29.860 --> 01:09:32.460
with twists and turns
and frights.

1085
01:09:32.500 --> 01:09:35.330
Not to mention some personal
growth for our hero.

1086
01:09:35.370 --> 01:09:36.740
What?

1087
01:09:36.770 --> 01:09:38.300
Go to the gym. Warn everyone.

1088
01:09:38.340 --> 01:09:39.770
Tell them to barricade
the school.

1089
01:09:39.800 --> 01:09:40.970
Where are you going?

1090
01:09:41.010 --> 01:09:42.640
To find someplace to write.

1091
01:09:42.670 --> 01:09:43.840
Slappy's going to come for me.

1092
01:09:43.880 --> 01:09:45.480
I have a deadline, literally.

1093
01:09:45.510 --> 01:09:47.550
Now go.

1094
01:09:50.380 --> 01:09:51.950
Unbelievable.

1095
01:09:51.980 --> 01:09:53.690
<i>? Off, off, off</i>

1096
01:09:53.720 --> 01:09:56.390
<i>? Off with your head</i>

1097
01:09:56.420 --> 01:09:59.860
<i>? Dance, dance Till you're dead?</i>

1098
01:09:59.890 --> 01:10:03.360
<i>? Heads will roll
Heads will roll?</i>

1099
01:10:04.530 --> 01:10:07.400
<i>? Heads will roll On the floor?</i>

1100
01:10:07.430 --> 01:10:08.630
Excuse me.

1101
01:10:08.670 --> 01:10:10.840
Sorry. Coming through.

1102
01:10:10.870 --> 01:10:12.840
Come on. We gotta get
to the stage.

1103
01:10:15.410 --> 01:10:18.810
<i>? Heads will roll
Heads will roll?</i>

1104
01:10:18.840 --> 01:10:21.480
<i>? Heads will roll On the floor?</i>

1105
01:10:24.380 --> 01:10:26.480
So this is what
a high-school dance is like.

1106
01:10:26.520 --> 01:10:30.790
Uh, yeah.
Usually the dancing's better.

1107
01:10:30.820 --> 01:10:32.320
But you get the idea.

1108
01:10:36.860 --> 01:10:38.630
That what they call dancing now?

1109
01:10:38.660 --> 01:10:41.030
I'm not sure. Zach.

1110
01:10:41.070 --> 01:10:42.830
- Mom. Mom.
- Zach.

1111
01:10:42.870 --> 01:10:45.070
I was so worried. I couldn't
get hold of you or Lorraine.

1112
01:10:45.100 --> 01:10:47.070
I know. I know.
Mom, everyone here is in danger.

1113
01:10:47.110 --> 01:10:50.410
We have to barricade the school.
Oh, no, Zach. Not this again.

1114
01:10:50.440 --> 01:10:53.080
He's telling you the truth.
I'm Hannah. I live next door.

1115
01:10:53.110 --> 01:10:55.350
All right.

1116
01:10:55.380 --> 01:10:58.080
Okay, everyone, listen up. Okay?

1117
01:10:58.120 --> 01:11:00.690
Okay. Everybody,
you gotta listen up...

1118
01:11:00.720 --> 01:11:02.850
Champ, get down.
I have something to say.

1119
01:11:02.890 --> 01:11:05.560
Uh... wow.

1120
01:11:05.590 --> 01:11:07.690
Okay, um...

1121
01:11:07.730 --> 01:11:09.560
Uh, okay, uh...

1122
01:11:09.590 --> 01:11:11.460
Listen to my best friend Zach.

1123
01:11:11.500 --> 01:11:13.670
Just... Just tell them.
Thanks, Champ.

1124
01:11:13.700 --> 01:11:15.800
Yeah. Yeah. All right. Um...

1125
01:11:17.970 --> 01:11:19.700
This is going to sound insane,

1126
01:11:19.740 --> 01:11:23.610
but monsters
have invaded Madison.

1127
01:11:25.610 --> 01:11:26.750
Guys, it's the truth. Okay?

1128
01:11:26.780 --> 01:11:28.610
He's telling the truth. It's...

1129
01:11:28.650 --> 01:11:30.380
He's not making this up.

1130
01:11:30.420 --> 01:11:32.420
They've blocked every road
out of town,

1131
01:11:32.450 --> 01:11:34.520
they've torn down
the cell towers,

1132
01:11:34.550 --> 01:11:38.790
and we've been cut off
from the rest of the world.

1133
01:11:38.820 --> 01:11:40.930
And they could be coming for us
any second,

1134
01:11:40.960 --> 01:11:42.530
so we need to work to...

1135
01:11:42.560 --> 01:11:44.600
Aah! He's right.

1136
01:11:44.630 --> 01:11:48.900
It's the Boogeyman.
And he's picking his nose.

1137
01:11:55.640 --> 01:11:56.840
- I'm not making...
- Aah!

1138
01:11:56.880 --> 01:11:58.480
There's a giant bug,

1139
01:11:58.510 --> 01:12:00.410
and it's eating
everybody's cars!

1140
01:12:00.450 --> 01:12:03.150
Uh, it's getting old, dude.
No, seriously!

1141
01:12:09.990 --> 01:12:12.760
They're here.

1142
01:12:12.790 --> 01:12:14.860
Whoa.

1143
01:12:17.700 --> 01:12:19.160
Ha, ha!

1144
01:12:19.200 --> 01:12:21.900
Now, this is a real homecoming.

1145
01:12:33.480 --> 01:12:35.810
All right. Everyone, everyone,
everyone calm down. Okay?

1146
01:12:35.850 --> 01:12:39.950
I know... I know what to do,
but I can't do it by myself.

1147
01:12:39.980 --> 01:12:41.520
Take this.

1148
01:12:41.550 --> 01:12:44.560
Invite the rest of our friends
to the party.

1149
01:12:50.160 --> 01:12:52.930
<i>Look. Those things out there,</i>

1150
01:12:52.960 --> 01:12:54.930
they're R.L. Stine's monsters.

1151
01:12:54.970 --> 01:12:56.530
He's here, and he can fix this,

1152
01:12:56.570 --> 01:12:58.540
but we need to buy him
time to write.

1153
01:12:58.570 --> 01:13:00.940
And don't worry,
he's a very quick writer.

1154
01:13:00.970 --> 01:13:05.510
The night was cold.

1155
01:13:07.110 --> 01:13:08.980
Cold was the night.

1156
01:13:19.960 --> 01:13:22.030
Come close. Don't be shy.

1157
01:13:22.060 --> 01:13:25.930
You don't wanna miss the show.

1158
01:13:29.730 --> 01:13:31.970
All right, everyone.
These are all the exits.

1159
01:13:32.000 --> 01:13:33.940
Find anything you can
to barricade the doors,

1160
01:13:33.970 --> 01:13:35.670
because we cannot let
the monsters inside.

1161
01:13:35.710 --> 01:13:37.540
Come on, guys.
We don't have a lot of time.

1162
01:13:37.580 --> 01:13:39.140
Stack them up there.
Stack them up.

1163
01:13:39.180 --> 01:13:41.850
Come on, quickly. Quickly. Yes.

1164
01:13:48.890 --> 01:13:51.760
All my friends in one place.

1165
01:13:51.790 --> 01:13:53.890
I've never been so happy.

1166
01:13:53.930 --> 01:13:56.260
I don't want this day to end.

1167
01:13:56.290 --> 01:13:59.160
And it doesn't have to...

1168
01:13:59.200 --> 01:14:03.200
as long as we get rid of Stine.

1169
01:14:03.230 --> 01:14:04.200
Charge!

1170
01:14:04.240 --> 01:14:06.640
Woo-hoo!

1171
01:14:34.170 --> 01:14:37.670
Go, go, go!
It's not gonna hold! Go!

1172
01:14:37.700 --> 01:14:39.270
Go, go, go!

1173
01:14:44.810 --> 01:14:46.910
We come in peace.

1174
01:14:46.950 --> 01:14:49.210
We come in peace.

1175
01:14:58.590 --> 01:15:01.560
We should be helping.
We should be leaving.

1176
01:15:04.800 --> 01:15:07.130
Uh... whoa.

1177
01:15:07.170 --> 01:15:09.030
What? What?

1178
01:15:09.070 --> 01:15:10.800
Where are you going?

1179
01:15:10.840 --> 01:15:13.100
We are so... through.

1180
01:15:18.880 --> 01:15:21.750
Please, no. Please.

1181
01:15:22.850 --> 01:15:25.020
No, please.

1182
01:15:48.110 --> 01:15:50.340
Oh, my God. How'd you do that?

1183
01:15:50.380 --> 01:15:52.340
Oh, um...

1184
01:15:52.380 --> 01:15:54.610
Silver fillings.
I have a ton of cavities.

1185
01:15:54.650 --> 01:15:57.120
When I was 10, I didn't brush
my teeth for a whole year.

1186
01:15:59.950 --> 01:16:01.950
Ugh, werewolf hair. Oh.

1187
01:16:05.120 --> 01:16:06.960
You saved my life, Chump.

1188
01:16:06.990 --> 01:16:08.830
It's actually "Champ."

1189
01:16:18.200 --> 01:16:20.370
I was just gonna say
"hug me again,"

1190
01:16:20.410 --> 01:16:23.140
but yeah, yeah, that works too.

1191
01:16:31.820 --> 01:16:34.150
We can't keep this up.
There's too many.

1192
01:16:34.190 --> 01:16:36.220
We have to get to Stine.

1193
01:16:36.250 --> 01:16:37.990
Let's go. Okay.

1194
01:16:38.020 --> 01:16:40.890
All the monsters had converged.

1195
01:16:40.930 --> 01:16:43.760
The vicious vampire bats,

1196
01:16:43.800 --> 01:16:46.000
the praying mantis,

1197
01:16:46.030 --> 01:16:47.670
the haunted mask...

1198
01:16:47.700 --> 01:16:49.700
Forgetting somebody?

1199
01:16:49.730 --> 01:16:50.870
Slappy.

1200
01:16:52.170 --> 01:16:53.440
How did you find me?

1201
01:16:55.310 --> 01:16:57.740
I know you. I created you.

1202
01:16:57.780 --> 01:16:59.940
Or is it the other way around?

1203
01:16:59.980 --> 01:17:02.150
I always forget.
We're so similar.

1204
01:17:03.480 --> 01:17:04.880
Slappy?

1205
01:17:04.920 --> 01:17:07.190
Slappy?

1206
01:17:07.220 --> 01:17:08.890
Slappy?

1207
01:17:08.920 --> 01:17:10.790
Slappy? Hi.

1208
01:17:13.120 --> 01:17:15.260
"Everyone in the high school

1209
01:17:15.290 --> 01:17:19.160
joined forces to defeat
Slappy and his monsters."

1210
01:17:19.200 --> 01:17:23.400
Hmm. But Slappy had other ideas.

1211
01:17:23.430 --> 01:17:24.430
No.

1212
01:17:26.970 --> 01:17:29.170
Dad!

1213
01:17:31.880 --> 01:17:33.340
Are you okay?

1214
01:17:33.380 --> 01:17:34.950
That dumb dummy
broke my fingers.

1215
01:17:34.980 --> 01:17:37.020
I was almost finished.
Only one or two pages left.

1216
01:17:37.050 --> 01:17:39.480
Well, forget two pages.
Write two words: "the end."

1217
01:17:39.520 --> 01:17:41.350
It doesn't work like that.

1218
01:17:41.390 --> 01:17:43.450
<i>School-wide announcement:</i>

1219
01:17:43.490 --> 01:17:45.160
<i>Monsters have overwhelmed
Madison High.</i>

1220
01:17:45.190 --> 01:17:47.890
<i>Retreat in an orderly fashion
to the storage room.</i>

1221
01:17:47.930 --> 01:17:50.930
I repeat, retreat in an orderly
fashion to the storage room.

1222
01:17:55.470 --> 01:17:57.970
We'll figure this out later,
all right?

1223
01:17:58.000 --> 01:17:59.470
Let's go. Follow me.

1224
01:18:00.810 --> 01:18:02.710
Come on, go!

1225
01:18:09.150 --> 01:18:12.180
Aah! Hannah. No.

1226
01:18:18.290 --> 01:18:20.460
Close it. Close it.

1227
01:18:35.410 --> 01:18:38.040
Are you okay?
Yeah. Yeah. Thanks.

1228
01:18:38.080 --> 01:18:39.310
Come with me.

1229
01:18:39.340 --> 01:18:41.910
Wait. Wait, she's a...

1230
01:18:41.950 --> 01:18:43.410
Yes, and I don't care.

1231
01:19:02.430 --> 01:19:04.570
All right. Come on, come on,
come on. Go, go, go.

1232
01:19:04.600 --> 01:19:06.870
Shut it! Go!

1233
01:19:06.900 --> 01:19:09.970
Get that door! Get it! Get it!

1234
01:19:10.010 --> 01:19:11.180
Oh, God.

1235
01:19:11.210 --> 01:19:12.910
Oh, God.

1236
01:19:12.940 --> 01:19:15.110
Wait. Mom, Mom, Mom. You okay?

1237
01:19:15.150 --> 01:19:17.320
Are you okay? Yeah.

1238
01:19:17.350 --> 01:19:18.850
What do we do?
They'll get through.

1239
01:19:18.880 --> 01:19:20.320
I don't know. I don't know.

1240
01:19:20.350 --> 01:19:22.090
Slappy wants me.

1241
01:19:22.120 --> 01:19:23.920
That's who he's after.

1242
01:19:23.960 --> 01:19:26.190
Listen to me, if I can lure them
away in one of those buses,

1243
01:19:26.220 --> 01:19:28.490
I know that they'll follow me
and you'll all be safe.

1244
01:19:28.530 --> 01:19:30.930
I'm coming with you.
No, I need to do this alone.

1245
01:19:30.960 --> 01:19:33.200
I've been running away
from people my whole life.

1246
01:19:33.230 --> 01:19:34.470
I was so angry at the real world

1247
01:19:34.500 --> 01:19:36.930
that I created
these terrible monsters.

1248
01:19:36.970 --> 01:19:38.470
Hold that door down.

1249
01:19:38.500 --> 01:19:40.070
But I'm not mad anymore.

1250
01:19:40.100 --> 01:19:43.070
It's my fault, not this town's.
Not yours.

1251
01:19:43.110 --> 01:19:45.840
There's gotta be another way.
Hannah, sweetheart,

1252
01:19:45.880 --> 01:19:48.510
it's time for me
to face my demons.

1253
01:19:48.550 --> 01:19:50.310
I believe in you. Shut up!

1254
01:19:50.350 --> 01:19:53.380
I'm sorry. I mean, shut up.

1255
01:19:58.460 --> 01:20:01.330
I have an idea.

1256
01:20:16.140 --> 01:20:17.440
Oh, Papa.

1257
01:20:17.480 --> 01:20:20.310
There's no escaping from us.

1258
01:20:22.210 --> 01:20:24.380
Bring him to me.

1259
01:21:25.380 --> 01:21:26.980
Did it work?

1260
01:21:28.750 --> 01:21:30.180
Not yet.

1261
01:21:30.210 --> 01:21:32.150
Come on. Come on, work.

1262
01:21:32.180 --> 01:21:33.420
Come on, come on.

1263
01:21:40.160 --> 01:21:41.560
Uh-oh.

1264
01:21:47.200 --> 01:21:49.300
Yes!

1265
01:21:49.330 --> 01:21:50.470
High five.

1266
01:21:50.500 --> 01:21:52.970
Oh, boy. Bad idea. Sorry.

1267
01:21:55.240 --> 01:21:57.510
Yes. It worked.

1268
01:21:57.540 --> 01:21:59.340
Oh, be careful, Zach.

1269
01:22:00.540 --> 01:22:02.210
We're gonna get through this.

1270
01:22:02.250 --> 01:22:03.380
Not a good time.

1271
01:22:03.410 --> 01:22:05.450
Okay.

1272
01:22:09.550 --> 01:22:12.060
Okay. Go.

1273
01:22:13.790 --> 01:22:16.690
Okay, it was clear there
was only one place left to hide.

1274
01:22:16.730 --> 01:22:19.230
I can't type while walking.
Then commit it to memory.

1275
01:22:19.260 --> 01:22:22.100
There was one place to hide.
It was the, uh, arcade gallery.

1276
01:22:22.130 --> 01:22:23.430
There is no arcade gallery.

1277
01:22:23.470 --> 01:22:26.570
Okay. That was, in fact,
the funhouse!

1278
01:22:26.600 --> 01:22:29.610
Wait, guys. Why don't we just
sit at one of these tables?

1279
01:22:29.640 --> 01:22:32.180
Come on. Guys!

1280
01:22:41.290 --> 01:22:43.150
Follow the scent.

1281
01:22:43.190 --> 01:22:45.720
Lead me to Stine.

1282
01:22:59.470 --> 01:23:02.640
Stine's ingenious plan
worked to perfection.

1283
01:23:02.670 --> 01:23:04.640
The funhouse was terrifying.

1284
01:23:04.680 --> 01:23:06.610
Not so much for Stine
as it was for the others.

1285
01:23:06.640 --> 01:23:09.080
But it offered refuge from
the real terrors

1286
01:23:09.110 --> 01:23:10.280
that lurked outside.

1287
01:23:10.310 --> 01:23:12.420
You wish.

1288
01:23:12.450 --> 01:23:15.790
He found us. Quickly, follow me.

1289
01:23:15.820 --> 01:23:21.130
Papa, you left
without saying goodbye.

1290
01:23:21.160 --> 01:23:22.690
Trying to hide from me?

1291
01:23:22.730 --> 01:23:25.160
That's like hiding
from yourself.

1292
01:23:25.200 --> 01:23:29.430
I was your best friend,
and you turned your back on me.

1293
01:23:29.470 --> 01:23:34.170
Locked me up, imprisoned me
in the pages of a book.

1294
01:23:34.210 --> 01:23:38.710
You stuck me on a shelf
for years and years.

1295
01:23:38.740 --> 01:23:41.310
The key was right there.

1296
01:23:41.350 --> 01:23:43.210
And you never used it.

1297
01:23:43.250 --> 01:23:46.520
You're not real, Slappy.
I created you.

1298
01:23:46.550 --> 01:23:49.390
I can write you out.

1299
01:23:49.420 --> 01:23:53.190
I've been saving this monster
just for you.

1300
01:23:53.220 --> 01:23:56.730
Say hello to my gelatinous friend.
Run!

1301
01:23:59.900 --> 01:24:04.200
It's The Blob That Ate Everyone.
Don't let it touch you.

1302
01:24:06.770 --> 01:24:09.140
We need to get to higher ground.

1303
01:24:09.170 --> 01:24:10.710
The Ferris wheel.

1304
01:24:14.780 --> 01:24:17.210
Zach, you go on ahead.
I'll hold it off.

1305
01:24:17.250 --> 01:24:18.350
You finish the book.

1306
01:24:18.380 --> 01:24:20.320
What? What do I write?

1307
01:24:20.350 --> 01:24:22.890
What's the end?
The story I've been writing.

1308
01:24:22.920 --> 01:24:26.360
It's what's happening right now.
You can do this. End it.

1309
01:24:26.390 --> 01:24:28.590
Wait.

1310
01:24:47.210 --> 01:24:50.350
Dad!

1311
01:24:51.920 --> 01:24:53.920
Hannah, he's gonna be okay,
all right?

1312
01:24:53.950 --> 01:24:55.490
We have to finish the book.

1313
01:24:55.520 --> 01:24:57.590
Okay.

1314
01:25:04.730 --> 01:25:08.130
Not so fun, is it?

1315
01:25:11.500 --> 01:25:12.640
Here we go.

1316
01:25:12.670 --> 01:25:14.540
Okay.

1317
01:25:15.840 --> 01:25:17.540
How do you like it, Papa?

1318
01:25:17.580 --> 01:25:22.250
The world is just outside
your grasp, but you can't move.

1319
01:25:22.280 --> 01:25:24.320
You're trapped.

1320
01:25:24.350 --> 01:25:28.550
That's what it felt like
to be locked inside your books.

1321
01:25:28.590 --> 01:25:32.660
Wait. The book. Where is it?

1322
01:25:36.590 --> 01:25:39.360
As the monsters converged,

1323
01:25:39.400 --> 01:25:40.870
Zach closed his eyes,

1324
01:25:40.900 --> 01:25:42.700
and the monsters were swallowed

1325
01:25:42.730 --> 01:25:44.840
back into the world
of paper and ink.

1326
01:25:44.870 --> 01:25:46.800
Can you type any faster?
This is my first time

1327
01:25:46.840 --> 01:25:48.440
using a typewriter. Keep going.

1328
01:25:52.840 --> 01:25:56.210
Eureka, eureka, 23-69...

1329
01:25:58.380 --> 01:26:00.250
They're coming.
What are we gonna do?

1330
01:26:00.280 --> 01:26:01.790
Finish it, Zach.

1331
01:26:01.820 --> 01:26:03.320
One by one,

1332
01:26:03.350 --> 01:26:05.460
the monsters disappeared

1333
01:26:05.490 --> 01:26:07.660
back into the book,

1334
01:26:07.690 --> 01:26:09.660
never to be seen...

1335
01:26:12.360 --> 01:26:14.900
again. The end.

1336
01:26:14.930 --> 01:26:16.870
Here. What happens now?

1337
01:26:16.900 --> 01:26:18.700
We're about to find out.

1338
01:26:34.520 --> 01:26:37.350
We're all gonna die!

1339
01:26:40.060 --> 01:26:42.330
Just hold on!

1340
01:26:42.360 --> 01:26:44.460
Hold on tight!

1341
01:26:46.630 --> 01:26:49.770
Where's the seat belt
in this thing?

1342
01:27:03.810 --> 01:27:04.950
Let's go.

1343
01:27:04.980 --> 01:27:06.680
Right.

1344
01:27:08.720 --> 01:27:10.920
I'm okay. I'm okay.

1345
01:27:10.960 --> 01:27:13.920
Okay. Hurry up. All the monsters
will be here any second.

1346
01:27:16.390 --> 01:27:17.430
All the monsters.

1347
01:27:17.460 --> 01:27:19.030
Wait. What are you waiting for?

1348
01:27:19.060 --> 01:27:21.870
Come on, open the book.

1349
01:27:21.900 --> 01:27:24.870
Hannah, there's something
that you need to know,

1350
01:27:24.900 --> 01:27:26.800
and you're not gonna...
Open the book, Zach.

1351
01:27:26.840 --> 01:27:28.010
No, no. You don't understand.

1352
01:27:28.040 --> 01:27:29.710
If we open the book,
that means...

1353
01:27:29.740 --> 01:27:33.040
It means I'll be stuck
on a shelf someplace forever.

1354
01:27:34.580 --> 01:27:35.810
You knew?

1355
01:27:35.850 --> 01:27:38.450
How many sweet sixteens
can one girl have?

1356
01:27:40.020 --> 01:27:42.890
Zach, it's time to move on.

1357
01:27:42.920 --> 01:27:46.660
Now open the book, scaredy-cat.

1358
01:27:49.090 --> 01:27:51.760
No.

1359
01:27:51.800 --> 01:27:54.060
Okay. Then I'll open it.
Wait, no. Hannah!

1360
01:28:06.740 --> 01:28:08.850
Wait, Hannah. I've got you.

1361
01:28:51.920 --> 01:28:53.990
Maybe if I hold on to you
tight enough...

1362
01:28:54.020 --> 01:28:56.490
You have to let go, Zach.

1363
01:29:11.780 --> 01:29:13.380
Whoa!

1364
01:29:24.660 --> 01:29:26.790
Slappy's not happy!

1365
01:29:26.820 --> 01:29:28.830
Neither is Stine!

1366
01:29:28.860 --> 01:29:31.900
Stupid dummy!

1367
01:29:33.630 --> 01:29:36.030
See you in your dreams!

1368
01:29:41.510 --> 01:29:42.910
You'll be okay.

1369
01:29:42.940 --> 01:29:45.210
I'll always be
in your imagination,

1370
01:29:45.240 --> 01:29:47.180
which is really where I belong.

1371
01:29:47.210 --> 01:29:50.680
I'm just sad we never
got to share a dance.

1372
01:29:59.260 --> 01:30:00.660
Wait.

1373
01:31:10.930 --> 01:31:13.130
Yeah. One more coat,
we should be good.

1374
01:31:13.160 --> 01:31:16.230
Let's go, ladies and gentlemen.

1375
01:31:16.270 --> 01:31:19.970
Welcome back to class, guys.
All right. Welcome back.

1376
01:31:20.000 --> 01:31:23.210
Hey. Watch it.

1377
01:31:23.240 --> 01:31:25.610
Back to business. Let's go.

1378
01:31:40.720 --> 01:31:43.530
Okay. I'll give you
a 60-second head start.

1379
01:31:45.000 --> 01:31:48.770
It's okay, Mom.
Let's go in together.

1380
01:31:54.670 --> 01:31:55.970
So mature.

1381
01:31:56.010 --> 01:31:57.340
You love it.

1382
01:31:57.370 --> 01:31:59.040
Maybe after fourth period.

1383
01:31:59.080 --> 01:32:00.740
Oh, okay. That would be great.

1384
01:32:12.120 --> 01:32:14.290
You okay? You breathing?
You're gonna be great.

1385
01:32:14.320 --> 01:32:16.960
Okay? You look great.
You smell great.

1386
01:32:16.990 --> 01:32:18.360
My God, what is that?

1387
01:32:18.400 --> 01:32:22.170
I rub myself in cilantro
every morning.

1388
01:32:22.200 --> 01:32:23.970
Of course you do,
my sexy little salsa.

1389
01:32:24.000 --> 01:32:25.200
Go on.

1390
01:32:25.240 --> 01:32:26.700
Okay. I'm off to work.

1391
01:32:26.740 --> 01:32:28.840
Oh, what did I have for you?

1392
01:32:28.870 --> 01:32:30.870
There it is.

1393
01:32:30.910 --> 01:32:34.110
Oh. Oh. Went too far. Got it.

1394
01:32:46.890 --> 01:32:48.990
Hello. Ahem.

1395
01:32:49.030 --> 01:32:51.700
My name is Mr. R. L. Stine,

1396
01:32:51.730 --> 01:32:54.260
and I will be your new
English teacher,

1397
01:32:54.300 --> 01:32:56.700
because Mr. Boyd is still
recuperating from injuries

1398
01:32:56.730 --> 01:33:01.870
sustained in a mutant-insect
attack.

1399
01:33:01.910 --> 01:33:04.270
Now...

1400
01:33:05.780 --> 01:33:07.710
every story ever told

1401
01:33:07.740 --> 01:33:12.080
can be broken down
into three distinct parts.

1402
01:33:12.120 --> 01:33:14.020
The beginning,

1403
01:33:14.050 --> 01:33:16.850
the middle

1404
01:33:16.890 --> 01:33:18.020
and the twist.

1405
01:33:20.190 --> 01:33:22.660
Hello, Mr. Stine.
Hello, Mr. Black.

1406
01:33:23.790 --> 01:33:24.900
Uh, who was that?

1407
01:33:24.930 --> 01:33:27.200
He's the new drama teacher.

1408
01:33:30.330 --> 01:33:33.400
Can I ask you something?
Of course.

1409
01:33:36.040 --> 01:33:37.310
Do you miss her?

1410
01:33:37.340 --> 01:33:39.740
Not a day goes by
that I don't think of her.

1411
01:33:39.780 --> 01:33:42.750
But she'll always be in here...

1412
01:33:42.780 --> 01:33:45.180
and in there.

1413
01:33:45.220 --> 01:33:47.780
And right here...

1414
01:33:47.820 --> 01:33:49.450
and in here.

1415
01:33:49.490 --> 01:33:51.660
And also right over there.

1416
01:33:59.830 --> 01:34:03.770
I may have written
one more book.

1417
01:34:12.510 --> 01:34:13.840
Hannah.

1418
01:34:17.250 --> 01:34:19.220
You're... You're real.

1419
01:34:19.250 --> 01:34:20.350
You came back.

1420
01:34:20.380 --> 01:34:22.350
I had to. You owe me a dance.

1421
01:34:30.130 --> 01:34:32.730
Come on, let's go.

1422
01:35:11.900 --> 01:35:14.100
You forgot about me.

1423
01:35:14.150 --> 01:35:29.700
<font color="#ffff80"><b>Hope it helped -> bozxphd</b></font>
